    "packageDtsBytes": 569344,
    "_packageDtsBytesWhy": "Raised to 569 344 B (556 KB) by design/14 §G, the DDL close-out (2026-09-01): 568 778 B measured, +15 161 B over F3's 553 617, same ceil-to-1 KB rule. Six declaration files move and the two that account for most of it are the two that gained a surface: `schema/extras.d.ts` 9 501 -> 17 707 B (the `exclude` node and its builder, `IndexExpression`, `StorageParameters`, the five index-option methods, and `IndexItem`'s new `expression` field) and `schema/column.d.ts` 16 250 -> 20 637 B (`.generatedAlwaysAs()`, `GeneratedAlwaysAsOptions`, `ColumnDdl.generatedAs`/`generatedAsFrom`, `PgEnumOptions.comment`). The rest: `query/meta.d.ts` +1 392 (`TableCodecMeta.generatedKeys` and the rewritten `insertableKeys` docblock), `session/copy.d.ts` +542, `schema/objects.d.ts` +336, `schema/index.d.ts` +97. This is a SIZE gate, not a type-performance one, and the type numbers say so: EVERY gated per-declaration and per-query check is byte-for-byte unchanged on both compilers (instantiations/column 3.08, /table 37, /relation 37.5, all-row-shapes 387, marginal/usage 40, all five per-query fixtures, all six schema-size ratios 1.000), and the headline moved 82 073 -> 82 476 on TS 5.9.3 and 133 996 -> 134 580 on TS 7 — +0.49 % and +0.44 % against design/12 §3 B's +2 % band and a 200 000 budget. Not one addition touches `ColMeta`, which is the rule design/11 §3 K2a states and the reason the numbers hold. Previously: Raised to 553 984 B (541 KB) by design/13 §5's F3 fix round (2026-08-30): 553 617 B measured, +2 705 B, same ceil-to-1 KB rule. All of it is declaration-file prose and four declarations: `TableCodecMeta.insertableKeys` (the insertable set COPY's default column list now reads, so it and the insert path cannot disagree), `CopyColumn.key`, `PgLikeClient.secretKey` and `PgLikeConnection.connect`/`cancel` (the parts of a `pg.Client` the protocol cancel drives itself, instead of `Client.prototype.cancel`, which reads the deprecated `activeQuery`). This is a SIZE gate, not a type-performance one, and the type numbers confirm it: headline instantiations 82 028 -> 82 073 on TS 5.9.3 and 133 822 -> 133 996 on TS 7 (+0.05 % / +0.13 %, against a 200 000 budget), every per-query fixture and every schema-size ratio unchanged. Previously: Raised to 550 912 B (538 KB) by design/12 §4 F1 (2026-08-29): 549 122 B measured, +11 579 B, same ceil-to-1 KB rule. All of it is `07` §6.1/§6.2's builder-level option methods — `.signal()` / `.timeout()` / `.outsideTransaction()` / `.withExecMode()` on `Query`, `GroupedQuery`, `SetQuery`, `InsertQuery`, `UpdateQuery`, `DeleteQuery` and `PreparedQuery`, 28 signatures with their JSDoc, plus `QueryRunOptions` and the `run` field on five builder state records. They are written out per interface rather than behind one `QueryOptionMethods<Self>` mixin precisely so the TYPE numbers do not move, and they did not: the headline instantiation counts are unchanged on both compilers (82 028 / 133 822), every per-query fixture is unchanged, and the largest movement anywhere in the report is +0.75 % on a schema-declaration arm (55 705 -> 56 124 on TS 7). This is a size gate, not a type-performance one. Previously: raised to 537 600 B (525 KB) after design/12 §4 P merged (2026-08-29): the statement-path gate and the encode-path rewrite added 1 219 B of declarations (537 543 B measured), same rule. Previously: raised to 536 576 B (524 KB) after design/12 §4 D merged (2026-08-29): the docs-found `valuesMany` guard fix and the pg-like seam declarations added 1 758 B (536 324 B measured), same ceil-to-1 KB rule. Previously: raised to 534 528 B (522 KB) at the design/12 round-A integration (2026-08-29): the merged tree measures 533 563 B, which is S's 504 595 B plus B's builder-gap declarations (query/types.d.ts 54 843 -> 72 190 B across B and S together: `$all`, the six join signatures and two laterals, `withRecursive`/`fromRaw`, relation `avg`/`min`/`max`, and 07 §1.3's four handle interfaces) plus K4's schema DSL (`pgDomain`/`pgSequence`/`pgExtension`, the index item options, `partitionBy`/`partitionOf`, `clusterOn`, `t.raw`). Each branch had passed its own raised number; the SUM is what ships, so the budget is set at the merged measurement by the same ceil-to-1 KB rule and ratchets from here. Previous step: raised from 409 600 to 524 288 B by design/12 §3 S, the session layer, measured 377 261 B before and 504 595 B after (design/07 §4.2's ~50 error classes, §1.3's handle interfaces, the src/session, src/observe and src/pooler declaration files). This is a SIZE gate and not a type-performance one: the headline instantiation counts moved +1.9 % over the whole round (80 485 -> 82 028 on TS 5.9.3), inside design/12 §3 B's +2 % band. tools/budgets.json gates the same bytes at 900 KB against design/08 §1.2 and passes; this number is the tighter of the two and still ratchets.",
